    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This podcast was created during fall quarter 2014 for PWR 2CG: Sounds of Stanford class at Stanford University. The podcast explores the theme of \"Breaking the 4th Wall\" as it applies to Stanford's ITALIC program, comics, and Chinese and American views on women majoring in STEM.\n\nIn Act 1, Diego Hernandez talks about life in the Stanford ITALIC program and how there is more to art than meets the eye.\n\nIn Act 2, Meagan Shinbashi discusses examples of racial stereotypes in comics and how they reveal things about ourselves that we wouldn't see otherwise. \n\nIn Act 3, Grace Geng discusses the cultural conflicts of being a Chinese woman majoring in STEM and what that reveals about views on woman in STEM.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
